id: DRAFT-libasd-forced-optional-python-submodule
trigger_tool: cmake|git|conan
phase: configuration,dependency_resolution,packaging
error_signature: add_subdirectory.*pybind11|downloading pybind11|pybind11.*CMakeLists.txt|git submodule.*update
severity: 3
category: build-system,dependency,cmake,conan
match_keywords: libasd,pybind11,submodule,release tarball,header-only,Python binding,CMake,add_subdirectory,optional component
title: Separate a header-only core when release CMake forces a missing optional binding submodule
root_cause: The release tarball omits the pybind11 submodule, but the top-level CMake path unconditionally enters extlib/python and add_subdirectory(pybind11); the documented C++ header-only core can compile independently, so the binding bootstrap should not define the core package boundary.
affected_scope: C/C++ projects that ship an independent header-only/core component alongside bindings whose release archives omit submodule sources while the root build unconditionally enables the binding.
verification_cmd: find . -path '*pybind11/CMakeLists.txt'; cmake -S . -B build; clang++ -std=c++11 -I. <core-consumer.cpp>
rec_priority: 1
rec_approach: verify-release-contents-and-package-core-component-separately
rec_description: Inspect the exact release archive and .gitmodules, reproduce the clean configure failure, then package only the independently documented core component with a real consumer test. Keep binding and upstream-suite status separate; never fetch an unpinned submodule or claim the whole project is adapted.
rec_command: test -f extlib/pybind11/CMakeLists.txt || true; cmake -S . -B build; conan create archives/l/libasd/1.5.6 -pr:h=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64 -pr:b=ci/conan/profiles/ohos-aarch64
rec_auto_fix: false
rec_impl: core-package-with-binding-boundary-evidence
fallback_priority: 2
fallback_approach: publish-pinned-binding-dependency-and-enable-binding-tests
fallback_description: If the Python binding is in scope, publish or otherwise provide a pinned pybind11 dependency through the approved Conan graph, patch the build only through the repository patch pipeline, and test the binding separately.
fallback_command: provide exact pybind11 source; cmake -S . -B build -D...; ctest --test-dir build --output-on-failure
fallback_auto_fix: false
fallback_impl: pinned-binding-dependency
forbid_1_pattern: git submodule update.*HEAD|git clone.*pybind11|curl.*pybind11
forbid_1_reason: An unpinned network/submodule fetch is not reproducible in clean CI and changes the release source boundary.
forbid_1_consequence: Builds become non-hermetic and can silently consume a different binding revision.
forbid_2_pattern: core.*passed.*Python|consumer.*passed.*upstream|skip.*Boost.Test
forbid_2_reason: Core consumer evidence does not prove Python binding or upstream Boost tests.
forbid_2_consequence: The PR overstates project coverage and hides a missing required component.
forbid_3_pattern: dummy.*pybind|empty.*pybind|stub.*pybind
forbid_3_reason: Fake binding headers or targets do not test the actual binding path.
forbid_3_consequence: CMake may configure while the requested binding remains unverified.
principles: P002,P003,P014
causes:
caused_by:
similar_to: E300,E342,E458
conflicts_with:
prerequisite_of:
